DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     vvmm__ppaaggee__bbiittss() calculates the bits representing the DEV_BSIZE range of
     bytes between _b_a_s_e and _s_i_z_e.  The byte range is expected to be within a
     single page, and if _s_i_z_e is zero, no bits will be set.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__sseett__vvaalliiddcclleeaann() flags the byte range between _b_a_s_e and _s_i_z_e as
     valid and clean.  The range is expected to be DEV_BSIZE aligned and no
     larger than PAGE_SIZE.  If it is not properly aligned, any unaligned
     chunks of the DEV_BSIZE blocks at the beginning and end of the range will
     be zeroed.

     If _b_a_s_e is zero and _s_i_z_e is one page, the modified bit in the page map is
     cleared; as well, the VPO_NOSYNC flag is cleared.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__cclleeaarr__ddiirrttyy() clears the dirty bits within a page in the range
     between _b_a_s_e and _s_i_z_e.  The bits representing the range are calculated by
     calling vvmm__ppaaggee__bbiittss().

     vvmm__ppaaggee__sseett__iinnvvaalliidd() clears the bits in both the valid and dirty flags
     representing the DEV_BSIZE blocks between _b_a_s_e and _s_i_z_e in the page.  The
     bits are calculated by calling vvmm__ppaaggee__bbiittss().  As well as clearing the
     bits within the page, the generation number within the object holding the
     page is incremented.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__zzeerroo__iinnvvaalliidd() zeroes all of the blocks within the page that are
     currently flagged as invalid.  If _s_e_t_v_a_l_i_d is TRUE, all of the valid bits
     within the page are set.

     In some cases, such as NFS, the valid bits cannot be set in order to
     maintain cache consistency.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__iiss__vvaalliidd() checks to determine if the all of the DEV_BSIZE blocks
     between _b_a_s_e and _s_i_z_e of the page are valid.  If _s_i_z_e is zero and the
     page is entirely invalid vvmm__ppaaggee__iiss__vvaalliidd() will return TRUE, in all
     other cases a size of zero will return FALSE.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__tteesstt__ddiirrttyy() checks if a page has been modified via any of its
     physical maps, and if so, flags the entire page as dirty.
     vvmm__ppaaggee__ddiirrttyy() is called to modify the dirty bits.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__ddiirrttyy() flags the entire page as dirty.  It is expected that the
     page is not currently on the cache queue.

     vvmm__ppaaggee__uunnddiirrttyy() clears all of the dirty bits in a page.

NNOOTTEESS
     None of these functions are allowed to block.

